/> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T14:37:03-07:00","id":1219795,"title":"","content":"I think the most accurate word here would be &quot;disappointing&quot;. But meant in a more universal, than personal manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T10:23:58-07:00","id":1221495,"title":"","content":"I realize I might be late to the conversation, but here is my 2 cent on the matter.<br /> <br /> The basic idea of the Abbey is that they are rich hedonist coming mainly from the top of society who view the supernaturals as subhuman, only existing for their amusement.<br /> Most people\u2019s problems come from the \u201cview as subhuman existing for their amusement \u201d part, witch even the book calls a minority (and in 2e anyone can get by the code/more of a slasher character type ) so lets focus on the other part.<br /> The are RICH hedonist coming from the TOP of society. Their chief weapons are money, connections, and social skills. Human society is a colossus that no supernatural wish to face, and they are at the wheels. They know the important people, have the financial power to motivate them, and should they be given a reason to exercise it, a wild imagination in employing those.<br /> <br /> But their true strength is in the fact that they talk to the monsters. They get to know them. They know what the monsters want, what they fear, who\u2019s allied to who, where are the fractures between them.<br /> Sometimes they hit those fractures sparking Supernatural wars and cleaning up the remainder when its done.<br /> Sometimes they offer a table to the quarreling sides to find a solution that doest have the common man between a raging werewolf and a frenzied vampire.<br /> Sometimes they share the fruits of humanity, open the gates of the privileged elite to them, making the part of High Society. And every Society has its rules. And without a higher authority to appeal to, it falls upon its members to enforce those rules. They can have the finest drinks and wildest parties, if they behave. If someone makes a habit of leaving corpses after himself they will find their invitees missing in short order and probably is made an example of.<br /> The best part? After they played mediator long enough and brought enough champagne to the parties, the monsters begin to like the status quo. And when something threatens it they themselves will take care of it.<br /> For the Ashwood Abbey the greatest weapons in the Vigil are the very creatures they hunt. Once man took the apex predator of his habitat and made it guard his children. No one says it cannot be done again, and if you try, you might as well enjoy it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24185-zsarnok","name":"Zsarnok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}